-- menu.flang — what the main menu's buttons do.
--
-- The screen carries this rather than each button carrying its own: a click
-- posts `:click:` to the widget, and then to the screen when the widget has no
-- script of its own (SCRIPTING.md, Events). One handler, one place to look, and
-- `src.id` tells the two buttons apart.
--
-- Play does not load anything. The level is already up and frozen behind the
-- menu — `pauses: true` in menu.fui is what froze it — so starting the game is
-- taking the menu off the stack, and nothing else. Hiding it also gives
-- mouse-look its cursor back, because `shows_cursor` stops being asked for.

def on_click(:click:, src ref) when src.id == "play" -> null
    hide_screen("menu")
on_click(:click:, src ref) when src.id == "quit"
    quit_game()
on_click(:click:, src ref)
    -- Any other widget on this screen. Nothing to do, and deliberately not an
    -- error: a decorative button added later should not take the menu down.
    return
end
